  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Rights of Indigenous and Quilombola Women: A Governance Matter</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s objectives is to promote the rights of indigenous and quilombola women in Brazil. The project will be implemented in the border states of Maranh&#xE3;o and Par&#xE1; with an expressive presence of both indigenous and quilombola communities living in forest areas (North and Northeast regions). UN Women draws on its strong partnerships with indigenous women&#x2019;s networks sustained since 2014 through the &#x201C;Voices of Indigenous Women&#x201D; group and with quilombola&#x2019;s CONAQ and will facilitate integration of their rights in governance processes, which directly affect them and their communities&#x2019; lives.</narrative>
  </description>
